>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (The May 2026 trip took place during a period of transition for Project Battambang. Due to the ongoing Thai-Cambodia border conflict and the increasing uncertainty surrounding the safety situation in Poipet, the committee sought guidance from our advisors, doctors and seniors regarding the direction of the trip. Through these discussions, it became clear that continuing on-ground operations in Poipet in the immediate future would not be feasible.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (As such, the May 2026 trip was redesigned as a recce and relationship-building trip based in Phnom Penh. Rather than carrying out a full-scale initiative, the trip focused on understanding the healthcare, educational and community landscape of potential new areas. Through consultation with the Cambodian Committee, Stung Meanchey and Koh Dach Island were identified as communities for exploration. These sites were selected as they allowed the team to assess different community settings, engage local stakeholders and consider where Project Battambang could contribute in a responsible and sustainable manner.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (The finalised itinerary was therefore structured around several key objectives: strengthening relationships with the Cambodian Committee, conducting door-to-door groundwork, engaging local NGOs, schools, hospitals and pharmacies, reconnecting with LADS scholars, and identifying possible long-term partners. Each component of the trip was planned to maximise opportunities for listening, observation and consolidation before any future initiatives are proposed.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
