<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (In May 2026, the Development team led primary data collection in Stung Meanchey and Koh Dach Island through door-to-door surveys, village chief meetings, school visits and engagements with NGOs that had prior experience in the area. These efforts aimed to assess community demographics, health profiles, educational needs, daily challenges and local priorities. They also helped the team evaluate the potential impact and feasibility of future screening or education initiatives.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Beyond data collection, Development also played a role in shaping the overall structure of the recce. This year, the subcommittee introduced a cross-committee schedule that integrated surveys, school visits and NGO engagements. This allowed different committees to contribute to the groundwork process while reducing survey fatigue and improving team morale. It also helped streamline operations and maximise productivity during the limited duration of the trip.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
