/E (This May 2026 trip was a pivotal one for the committee. As Project Battambang shifted towards Phnom Penh, many of the healthcare partnerships built over the years in Poipet could no longer be relied on in the same way. This brought new uncertainties, particularly in relation to referral pathways, medication sourcing and the feasibility of conducting future screenings in a new setting.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
566 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 239 0 R
/E (As such, the focus of this trip was not to carry out health screenings, but to lay the groundwork for future ones. The committee sought to form new connections with hospitals, pharmacies and local partners within Phnom Penh. These relationships are essential in ensuring that future screenings are not only well-supported on the ground, but also linked to appropriate follow-up care. Through these efforts, the Screening Committee hopes to better understand the local healthcare landscape and plan future initiatives that are practical, sustainable and responsive to the needs of the communities in Phnom Penh.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
