/E (As we moved beyond our longstanding school partnerships in Poipet, it became necessary to establish new connections with schools in Stung Meanchey and Koh Dach during this May Trip. Rather than implementing established programmes, the trip centred on listening, assessing and reconnecting. We sought to understand the educational landscape of the communities visited, while continuing to uphold our responsibility to existing LADS scholars by strengthening follow-up efforts with them. This served not only as a means of keeping in touch with our scholarship recipients, but also as an opportunity to evaluate the effectiveness and long-term impact of the programme.)
