/E (When we were able to return to Poipet, our engagement with the LADS scholars extended beyond financial support. Through LADS Camp, scholars came together to learn, bond and grow as young leaders within their community. Past camps focused on themes such as healthcare, leadership and community involvement, with activities ranging from health education sessions to games, skits and door-to-door visits. Scholars were encouraged not only to receive knowledge, but also to share what they had learnt with villagers around them. These initiatives helped strengthen their confidence, deepen their connection with one another and nurture their role as future changemakers in their own communities.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [7]
