/P 254 0 R
/E (Food and accommodation arrangements should continue to be planned with safety, accessibility and team welfare in mind. For days involving intensive fieldwork, catered meals should be arranged in advance to avoid delays and ensure that committee members are adequately supported. Where possible, accommodation with breakfast should also be prioritised, as this reduces morning logistical stress and allows the team to begin each day more smoothly.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (In relation to future screenings, Logistics should continue working with the Screening Committee and Cambodian counterparts to identify reliable pharmacy partners, medication sources and storage options in Phnom Penh. The management of existing supplies in Poipet should be handled with care, ensuring that Project Battambang remains respectful of its long-standing relationships while preparing for future operations.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
669 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (Lastly, collaboration with the Cambodian Logistics Committee should be strengthened through regular discussions before future trips. By involving the Cambodian team earlier in planning, Project Battambang can better anticipate local constraints, make more practical arrangements and build a more sustainable operational foundation for future batches.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
