<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (In collaboration with the Education Committee, Publicity also supported the filming of a short documentary featuring our LADS scholars and Bong Bondol. Even as Project Battambang explored a new base of operations in Phnom Penh, this initiative allowed us to remain connected to the communities we have long served in Poipet.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 258 0 R
/T (LADS: Documentary )
/E (LADS: Documentary )
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (Through candid interviews, LADS scholars shared their educational journeys, aspirations and reflections on how the scholarship has shaped their lives. Bong Bondol, a graduated LADS scholar and long-standing ground contact, also shared his experience of returning to serve his community after completing nursing school. His story reflects the deeper purpose of LADS: that education can empower individuals not only to improve their own lives, but also to give back to the communities that raised them.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (More than a publicity effort, the documentary serves as a bridge between donors, scholars and Project Battambang. By sharing these stories, we hope to close the loop between support and impact, reminding our community that behind every scholarship and every dollar raised are real people with real journeys worth telling.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
